the Apostle.\n27. Sunday. Tone 3 [Bz] / Tone 6 [Z]. Sixth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Pre-eternal.\" Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [bz]: \"Today they rejoiced.\"\n29. Tuesday. Tone 6 [Gz]. [Feast of] the Sons of Thunder (Boanerges). Barekendan [eve] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Wednesday. Tone 6 [Gk]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Blessed art thou, [Lord God] of our fathers.\" And the rest in order.\nJanuary\n3. Sunday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Seventh [Sunday]. Fast. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [ak]: \"Thy wondrous resurrection.\"\n4. Monday. Tone 4 [Bdz] / Tone 8 [Ch]. Fast. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers.\"\n5. Tuesday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Eve [Chragaloyts] of the Nativity of Christ.\nRoman Calendar of the Seven [Weeks].\nJanuary\n6. MONDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ. The post-feast season of eating (midjots oudisn) is twenty-one days.\n14. Tuesday. [Feast of] John the Forerunner.\n16. Thursday. [Feast of] Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and others.\n18. Saturday. [Feast of] Anthony, Tryphon, Barsama, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n19. Sunday. First [Sunday after Theophany]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: \"Dawn of the Only-begotten.\"\n20. Monday. [Feast of] Theodosius the King and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n21. Tuesday. [Feast of] Cyriacus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Gregory.",
